# ctx/

The typed context and the knot: the pure state machine at the waist of the bowtie architecture. The context is an immutable composite root threaded through transitions; the knot applies perturbations to produce new contexts and emissions. All state changes happen through this single point, making the core deterministic and replay-verifiable.

## Dirs

- `emission/` -- typed output events from the knot; each struct declares its tag and payload
- `perturbation/` -- typed input events to the knot; each struct declares its tag and data

## Files

- `ctx.ex` -- immutable composite root with typed slots and metadata overlay; threaded through the knot
- `catalog.ex` -- registry mechanism: closed membership, compile-time tag map, loud lookup on unknown tags
- `perturbation.ex` -- closed registry of 10 input types that drive knot transitions
- `emission.ex` -- closed registry of 10 output types emitted by the knot
- `knot.ex` -- pure function: applies perturbations to contexts, emits typed facts about what happened
